WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:01.303
- Alright, say goodnight guys.

00:00:01.303 --> 00:00:02.136
- Goodnight.

00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:03.224
- Goodnight.

00:00:03.224 --> 00:00:06.674
- I hope you have a good nighttime too.

00:00:06.674 --> 00:00:10.007
- (mumbles) nighttime too.

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:11.133
- He's copying me.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.633
(happy music)

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.795
- Hello my darling humans
I am Hannah dot mom

00:00:22.795 --> 00:00:26.765
and I'm here to talk
to you about mom stuff.

00:00:26.765 --> 00:00:28.070
(Hannah laughs)

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.292
Cool mom.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:30.389
We don't, I don't really
know what I'm doing

00:00:30.389 --> 00:00:33.189
thus far in the intro but
it's, but I'm here hi.

00:00:33.189 --> 00:00:35.494
Side note, look at what
Jackson made today,

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:36.744
it's a giraffe,

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.980
and a mouse, and a woman,
playing basketball,

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.356
I don't know, up to you.

00:00:45.356 --> 00:00:47.644
Anyway, let's talk about sleeping.

00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:51.017
Honestly, as a parent I can
tell you it freaking sucks.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.739
Every aspect of sleep having
to do with kids, sucks.

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:55.588
And if you're one of those people

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.662
who has kids who sleep through
the night, just go away.

00:00:58.662 --> 00:01:01.553
I'm just kidding you can
stay, I'm just very jealous.

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:04.157
Now my kids, are five and two,

00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:06.700
they sleep in their own room
they have their bunk beds.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.368
But I've been seeing a lot of my friends

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.074
on Facebook sharing their sleep situation

00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:13.898
and a lot of them practice
what's called bedsharing.

00:01:13.898 --> 00:01:15.811
Which means that the kids
sleep in the parent's bed

00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:18.920
every night, like they have
this huge king size bed

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.178
and all of the kids pile in
and it's like a big family bed

00:01:22.178 --> 00:01:24.465
usually there's a dog
at the foot of the bed.

00:01:24.465 --> 00:01:27.774
And they say it actually
helps the kids sleep better.

00:01:27.774 --> 00:01:30.273
And sleep in later, in the morning.

00:01:30.273 --> 00:01:33.226
I will try anything to
get my kids to sleep in.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.540
Because for some reason they're

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.237
just programmed to wake up
at the butt crack of dawn.

00:01:37.237 --> 00:01:40.565
So I spent the last week
letting my kids sleep in my bed.

00:01:40.565 --> 00:01:42.898
To see if it would
improve their sleep habit.

00:01:42.898 --> 00:01:45.698
And it did not turn out
the way I thought it would

00:01:45.698 --> 00:01:47.076
at all, whatsoever, but I learned a lot.

00:01:47.076 --> 00:01:50.099
So the ground rules for this experiment.

00:01:50.099 --> 00:01:53.232
First of all I gave them the
option to sleep in my bed,

00:01:53.232 --> 00:01:55.592
I didn't force them to
if they didn't want to.

00:01:55.592 --> 00:01:56.901
Because if they're cool just sleeping

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.665
in their bed for now, go for it.

00:01:58.665 --> 00:02:01.318
Second, I tried this
for seven days because,

00:02:01.318 --> 00:02:04.136
I think it takes a few days
to adjust to things usually.

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:06.402
And I wanted to make sure
that I gave it a fair chance.

00:02:06.402 --> 00:02:09.160
And the last rule is we didn't
change the bedtime routine.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.944
It was still bath,
brush teeth, books, bed.

00:02:11.944 --> 00:02:14.797
And then I'd go back out,
finish up what I was doing,

00:02:14.797 --> 00:02:16.056
whether it's dishes or gorging on

00:02:16.056 --> 00:02:19.242
ice cream while they're
asleep, I shouldn't admit that,

00:02:19.242 --> 00:02:21.055
and then come in and sleep with them.

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:24.638
Okay night one, I have
one taker, this guy.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.343
So night one was extremely
surprising actually,

00:02:29.343 --> 00:02:31.892
I presented the option to
both boys to sleep in my bed.

00:02:31.892 --> 00:02:34.820
And the only one who
wanted to was Wyatt, mister

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.251
independent, mister stay away from me

00:02:37.251 --> 00:02:39.527
mom, mister I want my own bed.

00:02:39.527 --> 00:02:43.514
It was amazing, he was so
cuddly, he was so sweet.

00:02:43.514 --> 00:02:44.347
What do you want?

00:02:44.347 --> 00:02:47.077
First of all he can't say
cuddles, so he calls it tuddles.

00:02:47.077 --> 00:02:48.364
- Tuddles.

00:02:48.364 --> 00:02:49.417
- Cuddles?

00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:50.270
- Yeah.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.719
- [Hannah] And the way that
he cuddles is he straight up

00:02:52.719 --> 00:02:55.916
like planks on top of
my body it's very weird

00:02:55.916 --> 00:02:58.289
and so I'm just like his human pillow

00:02:58.289 --> 00:03:00.294
and so that's how he likes to get tired.

00:03:00.294 --> 00:03:01.285
I love you.

00:03:01.285 --> 00:03:02.987
- I wuv you too.

00:03:02.987 --> 00:03:04.061
(Hannah giggles)

00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:05.019
- Say goodnight.

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:05.852
- Goodnight.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.767
- Goodnight.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.546
So we just did that,
cuddle, and I got to feel

00:03:09.546 --> 00:03:11.237
him fall asleep, and it was awesome,

00:03:11.237 --> 00:03:12.673
off to an amazing start.

00:03:12.673 --> 00:03:16.423
Okay, night two, we have
both takers tonight.

00:03:18.212 --> 00:03:20.116
So night two, Jackson caught on

00:03:20.116 --> 00:03:23.753
and he was like I want in on
this, so it was both boys.

00:03:23.753 --> 00:03:26.745
I was a little bit nervous
because it's a king size bed,

00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:28.819
but it's not that big for four people

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:31.280
and my kids are like not the smallest.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.560
So I was a little bit nervous
about how I was gonna fit.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.157
Bedtime was fine, they went to bed great,

00:03:37.157 --> 00:03:40.879
and then bout one am Wyatt wakes up

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:44.183
and decides that he doesn't
want to sleep in my bed anymore.

00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:49.079
Okay, we have one who's
requesting to go to his room.

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:52.420
Just a little change of heart I guess,

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.598
right, wanna sleep in your room?

00:03:54.598 --> 00:03:55.431
- Yeah.

00:03:55.431 --> 00:03:56.264
- Okay.

00:03:56.264 --> 00:03:58.108
So I come back in, go back to bed,

00:03:58.108 --> 00:04:01.067
wake up an hour later
to realize that Jackson

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:04.544
has literally taken over 95% of the bed

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.048
and I've been scooched over to like

00:04:07.048 --> 00:04:09.474
the closest you could possibly be to

00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:11.655
the edge of the bed without falling off.

00:04:11.655 --> 00:04:14.655
And honestly, with my husband
if he's like crowding the bed,

00:04:14.655 --> 00:04:16.698
or pushing me to the
side that's no problem

00:04:16.698 --> 00:04:18.549
cause I can just like
give him a little poke

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.909
in the ribs and he knows what that means

00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:22.425
and he scoots right over on his own.

00:04:22.425 --> 00:04:25.189
But with a kid, if you're
trying to move them

00:04:25.189 --> 00:04:28.224
when they're asleep it's
like holding a bomb.

00:04:28.224 --> 00:04:30.053
Don't wanna push the wrong button

00:04:30.053 --> 00:04:34.266
or like pull the wrong cord
and detonate this entire thing.

00:04:34.266 --> 00:04:36.030
So honestly moving him would've been

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.745
harder than just like sucking it up

00:04:37.745 --> 00:04:39.894
and continuing to sleep in my little

00:04:39.894 --> 00:04:41.877
cramped corner so that's what I ended up

00:04:41.877 --> 00:04:43.332
doing for the rest of the night.

00:04:43.332 --> 00:04:45.582
Okay, night three, I think.

00:04:47.112 --> 00:04:47.945
- Yeah.

00:04:47.945 --> 00:04:48.886
- Night three.

00:04:48.886 --> 00:04:50.079
- (mumbles)

00:04:50.079 --> 00:04:53.454
- So night three, both kids
were 100% in once again.

00:04:53.454 --> 00:04:55.693
But I don't know if it's just my kids

00:04:55.693 --> 00:04:58.027
or if this is like universal for all kids.

00:04:58.027 --> 00:05:01.109
My kids sleep in the
weirdest positions ever.

00:05:01.109 --> 00:05:03.877
Jackson's whole MO is to get as close

00:05:03.877 --> 00:05:05.751
to you as possible without like,

00:05:05.751 --> 00:05:09.128
actually physically climbing
inside of your skin.

00:05:09.128 --> 00:05:11.532
Wyatt likes to fling all over the place,

00:05:11.532 --> 00:05:14.187
and I swear it's intentional,
and after this night,

00:05:14.187 --> 00:05:15.600
was kind of the point where Matt

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.196
was like I think I've had
enough of this and I was like

00:05:18.196 --> 00:05:21.965
we're doing seven days,
and so we continued.

00:05:21.965 --> 00:05:25.230
Oh look who it is, okay do you remember

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:27.877
when you were sleeping
in my bed, how was that?

00:05:27.877 --> 00:05:28.710
- Good.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:32.180
- Good, so night four, it was just Jackson

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.015
and Wyatt kind of reverted back

00:05:34.015 --> 00:05:37.052
to his old ways of like I
wanna sleep in my own bed.

00:05:37.052 --> 00:05:39.278
Where do you wanna sleep?

00:05:39.278 --> 00:05:41.111
- I wanna pick a book.

00:05:42.126 --> 00:05:44.709
- Pick a book? Okay, goodnight.

00:05:45.984 --> 00:05:46.984
- Goodnight.

00:05:48.075 --> 00:05:51.202
- It was just Jackson,
night four, it was fine.

00:05:51.202 --> 00:05:54.392
Like I said Jackson's
like the most cuddly,

00:05:54.392 --> 00:05:56.574
but like in a burrowing type of way,

00:05:56.574 --> 00:06:00.373
so it's like getting into my
armpit and stuff like that.

00:06:00.373 --> 00:06:02.696
So I didn't sleep the
best, and he actually

00:06:02.696 --> 00:06:05.418
didn't sleep in any later than unusual.

00:06:05.418 --> 00:06:07.451
But it was, it was fine with just Jackson,

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:08.663
cause there's a lot more room.

00:06:08.663 --> 00:06:11.242
So night five, both kids
wanted to sleep in my bed.

00:06:11.242 --> 00:06:13.185
I guess Wyatt had a change
of heart or something.

00:06:13.185 --> 00:06:16.200
And they slept fine, I on the
other hand slept horribly.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.009
Interrupted sleep the entire night.

00:06:18.009 --> 00:06:19.545
I was exhausted the next day.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:23.517
Which is why on day six I
decided to take a little break.

00:06:23.517 --> 00:06:24.810
- Can I sleep in your bed?

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.529
- [Hannah] No I need a
little break tonight.

00:06:27.529 --> 00:06:29.072
Can you sleep in your bed tonight?

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:30.877
- (mumbles)

00:06:30.877 --> 00:06:32.770
- [Hannah] No, I need a little break,

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.193
there's no room for me in here.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.276
- Mama's bed, mama's bed.

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:40.789
- So yeah, I said I was
gonna do seven nights, but I,

00:06:40.789 --> 00:06:43.960
honestly, I just really
needed to get some sleep.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.375
Cause a cranky mom is
the worst kind of mom.

00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:50.261
Okay, one more night it is, right?

00:06:50.261 --> 00:06:51.146
- Goodnight.

00:06:51.146 --> 00:06:52.780
- [Hannah] So the seventh, and final,

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.238
night could not have come soon enough.

00:06:55.238 --> 00:06:56.854
Where are you sleeping tonight Wyatt?

00:06:56.854 --> 00:06:57.687
- My bed.

00:06:58.676 --> 00:07:00.525
- Your bed? Okay.

00:07:00.525 --> 00:07:01.646
Where are you sleeping tonight?

00:07:01.646 --> 00:07:02.479
- Mommy's bed.

00:07:02.479 --> 00:07:05.365
- And I was kind of like, I'd
had that really good night's

00:07:05.365 --> 00:07:07.001
sleep on night six so I was like

00:07:07.001 --> 00:07:09.345
I kinda just wanna
sleep by myself tonight.

00:07:09.345 --> 00:07:11.045
And guess where I'm sleeping tonight.

00:07:11.045 --> 00:07:11.878
- What?

00:07:11.878 --> 00:07:12.711
- [Jackson] On the bed.

00:07:12.711 --> 00:07:14.083
- The couch.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:17.311
And the funny thing is,
Jackson was fine with that.

00:07:17.311 --> 00:07:20.127
He doesn't actually care
if I'm in the bed with him.

00:07:20.127 --> 00:07:22.008
So I feel like I might need to reassess

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.295
his bed situation and like make sure

00:07:24.295 --> 00:07:27.917
that his bed is really
comfortable I'm really confused.

00:07:27.917 --> 00:07:28.917
Hi.

00:07:28.917 --> 00:07:29.750
- Hey.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.414
- Is your bed comfy, is
your bed comfortable?

00:07:31.414 --> 00:07:32.247
- No, no.

00:07:32.247 --> 00:07:33.080
- No, why not?

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.545
Is my bed more comfortable?

00:07:34.545 --> 00:07:35.378
- Yep.

00:07:36.736 --> 00:07:37.613
- How?

00:07:37.613 --> 00:07:38.780
- Because you.

00:07:39.662 --> 00:07:42.257
- So in conclusion, after
seven days of trying this

00:07:42.257 --> 00:07:44.125
experiment, I learned a few things.

00:07:44.125 --> 00:07:48.083
I learned first of all, that
bedsharing is not for us.

00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:50.530
It doesn't make my kids
sleep in any later,

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.748
doesn't make them sleep any better,

00:07:52.748 --> 00:07:54.471
I get a terrible nights sleep,

00:07:54.471 --> 00:07:56.524
my husband gets a terrible nights sleep.

00:07:56.524 --> 00:07:58.384
And I know that this works
for a lot of families,

00:07:58.384 --> 00:08:00.437
so if it works for you, great,

00:08:00.437 --> 00:08:02.266
I really wish it worked for me.

00:08:02.266 --> 00:08:03.845
We're just generally, all around,

00:08:03.845 --> 00:08:05.976
better off if we have our own space.

00:08:05.976 --> 00:08:08.363
Second I learned that the
one thing I really loved,

00:08:08.363 --> 00:08:09.924
about bedsharing, was just being

00:08:09.924 --> 00:08:11.681
able to spend more time with my kids.

00:08:11.681 --> 00:08:13.687
I'm at work every single day,

00:08:13.687 --> 00:08:15.841
I liked being able to get
home and have time with them.

00:08:15.841 --> 00:08:18.032
But then also be able to
spend the night with them

00:08:18.032 --> 00:08:21.193
and feel like I got to be
around them a little bit more.

00:08:21.193 --> 00:08:23.471
But honestly they're asleep, it's not like

00:08:23.471 --> 00:08:25.570
there's much interaction
or anything like that

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.268
so ultimately I think
we can live without it.

00:08:28.268 --> 00:08:30.015
And the third and final thing I learned

00:08:30.015 --> 00:08:31.696
is that I need to buy a new couch.

00:08:31.696 --> 00:08:34.733
Because ours is freaking
uncomfortable, as heck.

00:08:34.733 --> 00:08:38.483
Did not sleep the best,
not very comfortable.

00:08:39.648 --> 00:08:42.064
This ones up at the crack of dawn.

00:08:42.064 --> 00:08:42.953
(Hannah laughs)

00:08:42.953 --> 00:08:45.343
It is awful, it is not a couch suitable

00:08:45.343 --> 00:08:48.176
for anyone to sleep on, new couch.

00:08:49.315 --> 00:08:50.266
So that's all I got for today,

00:08:50.266 --> 00:08:52.291
and if you have any
experience with besharing,

00:08:52.291 --> 00:08:54.411
whether it's with your
kids, or with your parents,

00:08:54.411 --> 00:08:55.583
leave it in the comments, and if there's

00:08:55.583 --> 00:08:58.001
anything you want me to try in
a future episode for a week.

00:08:58.001 --> 00:09:01.354
Leave that in the comments
as well or you can text me,

00:09:01.354 --> 00:09:03.417
this is a real number I
do read every single text.

00:09:03.417 --> 00:09:05.217
I don't necessarily
respond to all of them,

00:09:05.217 --> 00:09:07.277
because I get a lot of them, but, I love

00:09:07.277 --> 00:09:09.858
to hear what you guys want
me to do in future episodes.

00:09:09.858 --> 00:09:11.564
And to all of you out there I wish you

00:09:11.564 --> 00:09:14.539
a blessed nights sleep,
wherever you're sleeping,

00:09:14.539 --> 00:09:16.126
whomever you're sleeping with.

00:09:16.126 --> 00:09:19.722
Have a good nights sleep, til next time.

00:09:19.722 --> 00:09:23.219
Well I have to say, I'm very happy

00:09:23.219 --> 00:09:27.386
to finally have the bed
to myself, it is all mine.

00:09:31.134 --> 00:09:34.816
And I'm so excited to get a
good nights sleep tonight.

00:09:34.816 --> 00:09:38.233
Is that mean, I don't know, I don't care.

